     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use under physician supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these common regimens?\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day), for mild to moderate pain\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **800 mg 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), for inflammatory conditions\n\nMaybe you meant 1,600 mg total per day. In that case I can enter 400 mg 4 times daily.\n\nIf you really do want the original dose, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first. Let me know which regimen you want and I'll enter it."
      }
